# Custom Select (required)

Never use native `<select>` in `apps/web`. Use the shared component:

```tsx
import { Select } from '../../../shared/components/Select';

<Select
  value={value}
  options={[{ value: 'a', label: 'Label', hint: 'Optional subtitle' }]}
  onChange={setValue}
  placeholder="Select…"
  icon={<SomeIcon />} // optional
  required
/>
```

## Rules

- Import from `apps/web/src/shared/components/Select.tsx` (admin may keep `AdminSelect` re-export).
- Style via `.ui-select*` in `design-v2.css` — do not invent per-page dropdown CSS.
- Prefer `label` + optional `hint` over cramming everything into one string.
- Because `Select` is not a native control, validate empty required values in submit handlers (`if (!value) setError(...)`).
- Specialized pickers (date range, reports chrome) may keep their own components, but general option lists must use `Select`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<select className="form-control" value={id} onChange={...}>
  <option value="">Select plan</option>
</select>

// ✅ GOOD
<Select value={id} options={planOptions} onChange={setId} placeholder="Select plan" />
```
